Apply the MSVC C runtime mode of a Rust target to its whole configuration, and give it to rustc.

A cc toolchain can select the CRT mode only from `--features`, for each configuration. The MSVC toolchain of `@llvm`
does, and it builds one libc++ archive for each configuration in that mode. So a `static_link_msvcrt` feature on a
target alone does not change its link. rustc also needs `-Ctarget-feature=+crt-static` for each crate of the graph, or
the crates name the dynamic C runtime.

The transitions of the Rust rules copy a `static_link_msvcrt` feature of the target to `--features`, with
`-dynamic_link_msvcrt`. A `-Ctarget-feature=+crt-static` in the `rustc_flags` of the target asks for the same CRT
mode. A target that asks for neither keeps its configuration. For an MSVC target, rustc then gets
`-Ctarget-feature=+crt-static` when the configuration has `static_link_msvcrt`. A crate for another ABI does not get
it, because `+crt-static` links glibc statically.

A proc-macro is a DLL that the host rustc loads, so it always takes the dynamic C runtime: on MSVC, rustc gets
`-Ctarget-feature=-crt-static` after the flags of the target. `rust_proc_macro` has no transition, and its flags can
hold a `+crt-static` that the crates of a product share, which would make it name the static C runtime.
diff --git a/rust/private/rust.bzl b/rust/private/rust.bzl
--- a/rust/private/rust.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/rust.bzl
@@ -67,6 +67,40 @@
 # Setting path for per_crate_rustc_flag, used in transition definitions
 _PER_CRATE_FLAG_SETTING = "@rules_rust//rust/settings:per_crate_rustc_flag"
 
+_FEATURES_SETTING = "//command_line_option:features"
+
+# The cc toolchain enables `dynamic_link_msvcrt` by default, and both features select the same CRT mode.
+_STATIC_MSVC_CRT_FEATURES = ["static_link_msvcrt", "-dynamic_link_msvcrt"]
+
+def _asks_for_crt_static(rustc_flags):
+    """Whether `rustc_flags` enable the `crt-static` target feature, in any spelling of `-C target-feature=`."""
+    values = []
+    for index, flag in enumerate(rustc_flags):
+        if flag in ("-C", "--codegen") and index + 1 < len(rustc_flags):
+            values.append(rustc_flags[index + 1])
+        elif flag.startswith("-C"):
+            values.append(flag.removeprefix("-C"))
+        elif flag.startswith("--codegen="):
+            values.append(flag.removeprefix("--codegen="))
+    target_features = []
+    for value in values:
+        if value.startswith("target-feature="):
+            target_features.extend(value.removeprefix("target-feature=").split(","))
+    return "+crt-static" in target_features
+
+def _msvc_crt_features(settings, attr):
+    """The `--features` of a target, with the MSVC C runtime mode that the target asks for.
+
+    A cc toolchain can select the CRT mode only from `--features`, for each configuration. So copy a
+    `static_link_msvcrt` feature of the target to `--features`, and the whole dependency graph takes the same CRT mode.
+    A `-Ctarget-feature=+crt-static` in the `rustc_flags` of the target asks for the same mode. A target that asks for
+    neither keeps its configuration.
+    """
+    features = settings[_FEATURES_SETTING]
+    if "static_link_msvcrt" not in attr.features and not _asks_for_crt_static(getattr(attr, "rustc_flags", [])):
+        return features
+    return features + [feature for feature in _STATIC_MSVC_CRT_FEATURES if feature not in features]
+
 def _toolchain_make_variables(ctx):
     make_variables = {}
     for toolchain_target in getattr(ctx.attr, "toolchains", []):
